                             CredXChanger v1.0
                             -----------------

 Well, let's start up whith a short history :). With all the Timebank-utils
 around, all of them missed something that I wanted. One day I came across
 a tool that allowed the users to exchange between different cred-types.
 So I thought to combine that idea, with a timebank, and added the possibility 
 to lend files/bytes, gamble for extra time, lend creds to a another user, 
 and to lose/gain creds due to interest.


                               What's done?
                               ------------

 1.0	This is the 1st version of course, nothing to say, other than
	thanks to Master Snille, SysOp at Oves Sommarhus, for the idea!


                    How to Install, and configure etc..
                    -----------------------------------

 The main program, CredX, you just install as any ordinary C-pfile!

 The maintenance program, CredMaint, takes 3 command-line arguments.

  1. all - subtracts/add the interest for deposited time and lent files 'n 
           bytes + reset the gambling stats, so the user get's another 10
	   fresh time at each game.

  2. int - Just fixes the interest. 

  3. game- Set's the number of plays to 0.

 The CredMaint scan your sysdata: dir for ALL accounts, so it's best
 to runit as an event!

 The configprogram ,ConfigCredX, got it's huge size 'cause it was written
 in C++, and those programs get BIG! But, you gain a lot of time writing!
 The different options is

  Interest:     The interest the user should get for both loans and deposits.
	        Should be typed in as an integer, i.e 25 => 25% => .25!
  File to byte: How many bytes the user gets from every file, i.e 10 gives
		the user 10 bytes for every file he/she exchange!
  Time to byte: How many bytes the user gets from every minute, i.e 10 gives
		the user 10 bytes for every minute he/she exchange!
  Max byteloan: How many bytes a user can lend as most!
  Max fileloan: How many files a user can lend as most!
  Max timesave: How many minutes a user as most can deposit!


                               Who dunnit!?
                               ------------

 CredXChange was written by me, Stefan Lindstrom AKA Wolverine, compiled
 with SAS C 6.51, tested with CNet 3.05 on an A500, with 3megs of RAM, 
 and 120 MB HD.


